# Constitution

## MUST

| Rule | Detail |
|------|--------|
| Role-based locators | `getByRole` → label/placeholder → text → `getByTestId`; locators in POM constructors |
| Web-first assertions | `expect(locator).…`; no raw DOM or fixed waits for readiness |
| `storageState` auth | Reuse fixture auth; never log in per test |
| Unique self-cleaning data | Faker-unique names; delete what you create in the same test |
| One tag per test | Exactly one of `@smoke` `@sanity` `@regression` `@api` `@e2e` `@destructive` on each `test()` |

## SHOULD

| Rule | Detail |
|------|--------|
| Faker factories | Shared factories for test entities |
| Enums for repeated strings | Route names, statuses, labels — no magic strings |
| JSDoc on action methods | POM actions document intent and params |

## WON'T

| Rule | Detail |
|------|--------|
| XPath | Role/label discovery only |
| `waitForTimeout` | Web-first assertions or action auto-wait |
| Hardcoded secrets | `process.env` or fixture auth |
| `any` | Proper types or narrow the value |
| Weakened assertions | Stop and report; never delete or soften to pass |
| Heal a real bug | Triage first; bugs → bug-reporter, drift → self-heal |
| Tags on `describe` | One tag per `test()` only |

## Agent governance

Behavioral governance for coordinator and subagents — **not hook-enforced**.
Follow before any non-trivial edit, delegation, or implementation.

### Audit-then-edit contract

1. **Audit** — read relevant code, skills, ticket/AC, and env docs before changing anything.
2. **Propose** — emit a Proposal block (below) and wait for the confidence gate.
3. **Edit** — implement only after the gate allows proceed.

Trivial tasks (typo fix named by user, single-line change with explicit instruction) may skip the Proposal block.

### Proposal block

Every non-trivial task emits this **before** editing:

```markdown
## Proposal

**Scope:** …
**Confidence:** N/10
**Rationale:** …
**Unknowns:** …
```

### Confidence gate

| Confidence | Rule |
|------------|------|
| **&lt; 5** | Do **not** proceed — ask for the missing input |
| **5–7** | Proceed only with explicit Unknowns listed **and** human approval |
| **≥ 8** | Proceed |

### Never invent

Never invent a path, enum, env var, credential, or message — **ask or explore** instead (read repo, `.env.example`, Jira, live UI via explore-and-generate / Agent-Browser).

## Skills & agents

**Skills:** `a11y-checks` (axe on UI tests) · `ci-failure-triage` (classify red CI) · `didaxis-bulk-cleanup` (bulk-delete programs) · `eval-report` (suite reliability report) · `explore-and-generate` (gap discovery → Gherkin) · `exploratory-charter` (feature + risk → charter & findings format) · `jira-bug-reporter` (failure → Jira) · `jira-ticket-to-gherkin` (ticket → Gherkin) · `playwright-api-fixture` (request + cleanup) · `playwright-assertions` (expects + snapshots) · `playwright-stability` (config + time) · `playwright-test-cleanup` (self-clean data) · `pom-conventions` (POM structure) · `programs-network-mocking` (programs edge cases) · `self-heal` (locator drift only)

**Agents:** `triage` (diagnose red runs) · `test-writer` (plan → spec) · `bug-reporter` (confirmed defect → Jira)
